    "body": "## Overview\n\nCache the `VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_ALGO` environment variable read in the custom all-reduce kernel, eliminating per-call `std::getenv` + `strcmp` chain overhead in the all-reduce hot path.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Eliminates per-call `std::getenv(\"VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_ALGO\")` in custom all-reduce\n- Eliminates per-call `strcmp` chain for algo parsing\n- Environment variable is read and parsed once per process via static local variables\n\n## Validation\n\n- Code review: the static local initialization is thread-safe in C++11+ (guaranteed by the standard). The all-reduce kernel is called from a single CUDA stream per process, so there is no race concern.\n- The behavior is identical: `getenv` returns the same value throughout the process lifetime, and the parsed `force_1stage`/`force_2stage` flags are deterministic from the env value.\n\n## Details\n\nThe custom all-reduce kernel in `csrc/custom_all_reduce.cuh` had a comment saying \"Check environment variable once\" but actually called `std::getenv` and ran the full `strcmp` chain on every `all_reduce` invocation. This is on the TP all-reduce hot path (2N calls per forward pass for an N-layer model).\n\nUse C++ static local variables to cache the `getenv` result and parsed flags. Static locals are initialized exactly once (thread-safe per C++11 standard), so subsequent calls skip the `getenv` + `strcmp` chain entirely.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
